From: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: sun55i-de: clamp RCQ arm target to leading blanking

The v35x RCQ latches ~immediately when armed and is not frame-gated, so
the arm must land in the vertical blanking. arm_target = vbp + 3% of
vtotal (vendor math) can exceed the leading-blanking size on modes with
a large back porch, placing the arm inside active video. Clamp it to
half the leading blanking, in raw (un-doubled) counter units like
arm_target itself. Matches the Armbian sunxi-6.18 7000 series.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
@@ -865,6 +865,13 @@
 	vbp = mode->crtc_vtotal - mode->crtc_vsync_end;
 	de->line_total = vtotal ? vtotal : 1;
 	de->arm_target = vbp + (vtotal * 3) / 100;
+	/*
+	 * Clamp the arm target to half the leading blanking so it can never
+	 * land inside active video (vendor targets ~line 69 at 1080p60).
+	 * Raw (un-doubled) units, same as arm_target itself.
+	 */
+	if (de->arm_target > (vtotal - mode->crtc_vsync_start) / 2)
+		de->arm_target = (vtotal - mode->crtc_vsync_start) / 2;
 	de->ns_per_line = clock ?
 		div_u64((u64)mode->crtc_htotal * NSEC_PER_MSEC, clock) : 0;
 
